    "MPPSC-2020-008": {
      "from": [
        "B"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "Coal India Limited has been a Maharatna since 11 April 2011, so it cannot be the answer to a \"does not fall under Maharatna\" question. The non-Maharatna CPSE in the list is Oil India Limited, a Navratna in 2010 and only elevated to Maharatna on 4 August 2023, long after the January 2020 list the question cites."
    },
    "MPPSC-2020-032": {
      "from": [
        "B"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "Kailash Satyarthi was born on 11 January 1954 at Vidisha, Madhya Pradesh, where he studied at the Samrat Ashok Technological Institute. The printed key (Sehore) is wrong; the question's own supplied explanation already said Vidisha."
    },
    "MPPSC-2020-054": {
      "from": [
        "A"
      ],
      "to": [
        "B"
      ],
      "basis": "The States Reorganisation Act, 1956 with the Seventh Amendment abolished the Part A/B/C categories and created 14 states and 6 union territories with effect from 1 November 1956. Eighteen states and nine union territories describe a later political map, not the 1956 Act."
    },
    "MPPSC-2020-076": {
      "from": [
        "B"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "Bhagwat Dayal Sharma was the first Chief Minister of Haryana (November 1966 to March 1967) and later Governor of Madhya Pradesh (30 April 1980 to 14 May 1984). Ram Naresh Yadav, the printed key, was Chief Minister of Uttar Pradesh, so the question's premise does not fit him."
    },
    "MPPSC-2020-095": {
      "from": [
        "B"
      ],
      "to": [
        "C"
      ],
      "basis": "PUMA in robotics expands to Programmable Universal Machine for Assembly, the Unimation/Unimation-Scheinman assembly robot. The printed key \"Programmed Utility Machine for Assembly\" is a reordered distractor; the question's own supplied explanation gave the correct expansion."
    },
    "MPPSC-2019-027": {
      "from": [
        "A",
        "B",
        "C"
      ],
      "to": [
        "C"
      ],
      "basis": "Section 6(2) of the Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993 makes a Member eligible for re-appointment for another term of five years, so the statement that a Member is not eligible is the only false statement. Statements A, B and D each reproduce the Act, which means the printed key A+B+C marked two true statements as incorrect."
    },
    "MPPSC-2019-046": {
      "from": [
        "C"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "Karewas are the lacustrine and glacial clay terraces of the Kashmir valley floor, where saffron is grown, not a landform of the Himachal-Uttarakhand Himalaya. The printed key named the Himachal-Uttarakhand Himalaya, which contradicts both the standard geomorphology and the paper's own explanation."
    },
    "MPPSC-2019-060": {
      "from": [
        "C"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "Kathi is a folk dance of the Nimar region of Madhya Pradesh, performed by the Balai community from Dev Prabodhini Ekadashi to Mahashivratri in worship of Parvati. The decorated bamboo kathi is the prop the dancers carry, so 'wooden art' names the object rather than what Kathi is."
    },
    "MPPSC-2019-074": {
      "from": [
        "B"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "A keyboard is an input device, so the group keyboard-printer-monitor is not made up only of output devices. Plotter, printer and monitor are all outputs, which is the correct answer."
    },
    "MPPSC-2019-097": {
      "from": [
        "A"
      ],
      "to": [
        "D"
      ],
      "basis": "Old NH-3 ran from Agra through Gwalior, Shivpuri, Guna, Dewas and Indore to Mumbai and carried about 712 km in Madhya Pradesh, old NH-12 and old NH-7 also entered the state, but NH-8 ran from Delhi through Jaipur, Udaipur, Ahmedabad and Vadodara to Mumbai without passing through Madhya Pradesh."
    },
    "MPPSC-2017-100": {
      "from": [
        "B"
      ],
      "to": [
        "C"
      ],
      "basis": "The IMF lends only to its member countries, not only to developed countries. The stored key B is contradicted by the paper's own explanation and by the identical question at number 85, which the same paper keys C."
    }
